    "caption": "Inspect the supplied high-resolution T2 mean and two manual hippocampal annotation sets from one healthy-adult research participant. All native planes, components and label-cell boundaries are retained. Compare rater differences without treating either annotation as anatomical truth. Annotations are tied to the prepared mean; raw repetitions remain separate image-only views. This does not establish diagnosis, normal-volume thresholds or complete reporting anatomy.",
    "attribution": "Clark, Ian A.; Maguire, Eleanor A. (2023). Release of cognitive and multimodal MRI data including real-world tasks and hippocampal subfield segmentations. Dryad version7, DOI10.5061/dryad.2v6wwpzt3. Source publication: Scientific Data10:540, DOI10.1038/s41597-023-02449-9. CC0-1.0.\n\nSelected source: Main Sample participant10 and DICE participant10. Primer adaptations: lossless native-plane transport, separate manual label schematics and complete source voxel-cell boundaries. No additional source resampling, smoothing or component deletion. The prepared mean retains its original intensity scale. Both annotation folders contain identical reference-image bytes. Annotations belong to the prepared mean; raw-repetition anatomical registration is unverified. Files0009 and0010 are byte-identical.\n\nThese are research source annotations, not histological truth, a normal-population standard, a current-patient registration or complete clinical reporting coverage. Source combined labels remain combined. The source Cyst category appears only in the reliability annotation and is not independently diagnosed here.\n",
